\DOC ASSERT_USING_ASM_ARITH_TAC

\TYPE {ASSERT_USING_ASM_ARITH_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Adds a supplied arithmetic term to the goal's assumptions as a new assumption,
leaving a single subgoal.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {t : term} is the proposition to be asserted; it is a
(linear/numeric) arithmetic statement over terms available in the goal. The
conclusion is untouched, the new assumption is appended at the end of the
assumption list (with any type annotations in {t} dropped from the printed
assumption), and no proof obligation for {t} is left to the user.
{
        A ?- u
   ================ ASSERT_USING_ASM_ARITH_TAC t
      A, t ?- u
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this one kind of outcome occurs, on goals that
already carry a sizeable list of arithmetic and separation assumptions, with
asserted terms that follow arithmetically from them.

\ENDDOC
